  sections: [
    ['Oral and maxillofacial surgery', [
      '**Oral and maxillofacial surgery (OMFS)** treats diseases, injuries and defects of the mouth, jaws and face. An **extraction** (exodontia) is **simple** (a visible tooth removed with elevators and forceps) or **surgical** (requiring a flap, bone removal or sectioning the tooth). **Impacted teeth** are blocked from erupting, most often third molars and maxillary canines; impactions are described as **soft tissue** or **bony** and by angulation (**mesioangular**, **distoangular**, **vertical**, **horizontal**).',
      {t: 'table', head: ['Procedure or term', 'Meaning'], rows: [
        ['Alveoloplasty', 'Reshaping the alveolar bone, often before dentures'],
        ['Biopsy (incisional, excisional, brush)', 'Removing tissue for microscopic diagnosis'],
        ['Frenectomy', 'Removal or release of a frenum (such as for tongue-tie)'],
        ['Orthognathic surgery', 'Repositioning the jaws to correct skeletal malocclusion'],
        ['Open reduction / closed reduction', 'Surgically exposing and fixing / realigning without incision (jaw fractures)'],
        ['Incision and drainage (I&D)', 'Opening an abscess to drain pus'],
        ['Exostosis / torus removal', 'Removing bony growths'],
        ['Cleft lip and palate repair', 'Surgical correction of congenital clefts'],
      ]},
      'Post-extraction instructions: bite on gauze for about 30–60 minutes to form a clot, avoid spitting, rinsing vigorously, smoking or drinking through a straw for at least 24 hours, use ice packs the first day, eat soft foods and take analgesics as directed. **Alveolar osteitis (dry socket)** occurs when the blood clot is lost, exposing bone; severe throbbing pain begins 2–4 days after extraction, often with a bad taste or odor. Other complications: bleeding, infection, paresthesia (nerve injury), sinus communication after maxillary molar extraction and trismus.',
      {t: 'check', q: 'Three days after a mandibular third molar extraction, a patient has severe throbbing pain radiating to the ear and an empty-looking socket. This is most likely:', options: ['Alveolar osteitis (dry socket)', 'Normal healing', 'Periodontal abscess', 'Pericoronitis only'], why: 'Loss of the clot exposes bone, causing pain that begins 2–4 days after extraction.'},
    ]],
    ['Prosthodontics', [
      '**Prosthodontics** restores and replaces teeth with artificial substitutes (prostheses). **Fixed prosthodontics** are cemented or bonded and cannot be removed by the patient; **removable prosthodontics** can be taken out.',
      {t: 'table', head: ['Prosthesis', 'Type', 'Description'], rows: [
        ['Crown', 'Fixed', 'Covers the entire visible tooth; materials include gold, porcelain-fused-to-metal (PFM), zirconia and lithium disilicate'],
        ['Fixed bridge (fixed partial denture)', 'Fixed', 'Replaces missing teeth by attaching to prepared teeth on each side'],
        ['Complete denture', 'Removable', 'Replaces all teeth in an arch; an **immediate denture** is placed the same day teeth are extracted'],
        ['Removable partial denture (RPD)', 'Removable', 'Replaces some teeth, held by clasps and rests on remaining teeth, with a metal framework and acrylic base'],
        ['Overdenture', 'Removable', 'Denture fitted over retained roots or implants'],
        ['Implant-supported crown or bridge', 'Fixed', 'Attached to dental implants'],
        ['Obturator / maxillofacial prosthesis', 'Removable', 'Closes defects such as a cleft palate or replaces facial structures'],
      ]},
      {t: 'w', kind: 'match', title: 'Parts of a fixed bridge and dentures', pairs: [['Abutment', 'Tooth or implant that supports a bridge'], ['Pontic', 'Artificial tooth that replaces the missing tooth'], ['Retainer', 'Crown on the abutment that holds the bridge'], ['Connector', 'Joint linking the pontic to the retainer'], ['Clasp', 'Arm of a partial denture that grips a natural tooth'], ['Denture base', 'Pink acrylic part that rests on the gums'], ['Reline', 'Resurfacing the tissue side of a denture to improve fit']]},
      'A **three-unit bridge** replacing one missing tooth has two retainers (crowns on the abutments) and one pontic. Dentures need periodic **relines** or **rebases** because the alveolar ridge resorbs over time. Teach denture patients to clean dentures daily, remove them at night and keep them moist.',
    ]],
    ['Dental implants', [
      'A **dental implant** is a titanium (or zirconia) post placed into the jawbone to replace a root. Bone fuses directly to the implant surface, a process called **osseointegration**, discovered by Per-Ingvar Brånemark. Implants preserve bone, do not require preparing neighboring teeth and can support crowns, bridges or dentures.',
      {t: 'w', kind: 'order', title: 'The implant process', steps: ['Evaluation: exam, medical history, CBCT imaging and treatment planning', 'Bone grafting or sinus lift if bone volume is inadequate', 'Surgical placement of the implant fixture in the bone', 'Healing for osseointegration, often about 3 to 6 months', 'Abutment placement to connect the implant to the restoration', 'Impression or digital scan of the implant position', 'Delivery of the final crown, bridge or implant-retained denture']},
      'Parts: the **fixture** (screw in the bone), the **abutment** (connector above the gumline) and the **restoration** (crown). Risks include failure to integrate, **peri-implantitis** (inflammation with bone loss around an implant), nerve injury and sinus perforation. Smoking and uncontrolled diabetes increase failure risk.',
      {t: 'check', q: 'The direct structural and functional connection between bone and an implant surface is called:', options: ['Osseointegration', 'Obturation', 'Ankylosis of the PDL', 'Calcification'], why: 'Osseointegration anchors the implant like a root.'},
    ]],
    ['Cosmetic dentistry', [
      {t: 'table', head: ['Procedure', 'Description'], rows: [
        ['Tooth whitening (bleaching)', 'Peroxide gels lighten intrinsic and extrinsic stains; in-office (higher concentration) or custom-tray at home; temporary sensitivity is common; does not change crowns or fillings'],
        ['Veneers', 'Thin shells of porcelain or composite bonded to the facial surfaces of anterior teeth to change color, shape or alignment; porcelain veneers usually require removing a small amount of enamel'],
        ['Direct bonding', 'Tooth-colored composite applied to repair chips, close gaps (diastemas) or change shape'],
        ['Gingival contouring (gingivoplasty)', 'Reshaping gum tissue for a more even smile'],
        ['Enamel microabrasion / enameloplasty', 'Removing surface stains or reshaping enamel'],
        ['Smile design', 'Planning tooth proportions, color and gum line, often with digital mock-ups'],
      ]},
      '**Extrinsic stains** are on the surface (coffee, tea, tobacco, red wine) and respond to cleaning and whitening; **intrinsic stains** are within the tooth (tetracycline staining, fluorosis, trauma, nonvital teeth) and may need veneers, crowns or internal bleaching.',
      {t: 'w', kind: 'sort', title: 'Fixed or removable?', buckets: ['Fixed', 'Removable'], items: [['Three-unit bridge', 0], ['Porcelain veneer', 0], ['Implant crown', 0], ['PFM crown', 0], ['Complete denture', 1], ['Removable partial denture', 1], ['Overdenture', 1], ['Clear aligner retainer', 1]]},
    ]],
  ],
  takeaways: ['Simple extractions use elevators and forceps; surgical extractions need flaps, bone removal or sectioning; impactions are soft tissue or bony.', 'Dry socket (alveolar osteitis): clot lost, pain 2–4 days later; avoid straws, smoking and vigorous rinsing.', 'Fixed: crowns, bridges (abutment, retainer, pontic, connector), implant crowns. Removable: complete and partial dentures (clasps, base).', 'Implants: fixture, abutment, crown; osseointegration takes months; peri-implantitis is a risk.', 'Whitening removes extrinsic stains best; veneers and bonding mask intrinsic stains and shape changes.'],
